WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Let's look at how we adapt these skills for a child.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.700
Just like with adults, you only jump in if you see signs of severe obstruction, meaning

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.660
the child cannot speak, cry, or cough effectively.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:17.320
If they are coughing loudly, stay close and encourage them to keep at it until the object

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:18.520
comes out.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:23.780
When a child is choking, the most important first step is to get down to their level.

00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:27.200
Kneel or sit so your eyes are level with theirs.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:31.900
Not only does this keep them calm, but it ensures you are striking and pulling at the

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.919
correct angles.

00:00:33.919 --> 00:00:38.860
If you are standing, place one foot between theirs to keep yourself steady.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:45.020
Alternate between the two main actions, five back blows and five abdominal thrusts.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:49.459
Keep repeating this cycle of five blows and five thrusts until the object is ejected or

00:00:49.459 --> 00:00:51.139
the child becomes unresponsive.

